{
  "$comment": [
    "Provenance of every published release tag: where it pointed when it was",
    "published. Issue #386. A git tag is a mutable ref, so the commit a tag was",
    "ORIGINALLY published at is not recoverable from the API after a move - it has",
    "to be written down, which is what this file is.",
    "",
    "object_sha is the sha the ref points at: the annotated tag object where there",
    "is one, otherwise the commit. It is the value the audit compares, because an",
    "annotated tag object is content-addressed over its target, message, and tagger,",
    "so re-annotating the same commit still changes it. commit_sha is that ref",
    "dereferenced to the commit whose tree consumers actually install.",
    "",
    "This file's integrity comes from git history and branch protection on main:",
    "editing a recorded sha takes a reviewed pull request, while moving a tag takes",
    "nothing. Editing an entry to silence a red drift check is therefore a",
    "review-visible act, and is never the correct fix - see the recovery procedure",
    "in core/surface/skills/release/SKILL.md.",
    "",
    "Verified 2026-07-25 against BOTH the GitHub API and an independent local clone.",
    "Adding a tag here is a release step; see the release skill.",
    "",
    "ca-codex 0.4.1-0.4.9 and 0.4.12-0.4.13 never got a CHANGELOG section when the",
    "manifest was bumped: they are shared-core commits (also bumping ca's own",
    "manifest) whose payload-gate side effect never got a matching entry written",
    "into plugins/ca-codex/CHANGELOG.md. Backfilled 2026-08-08 by composing each",
    "section directly from that commit's own CHANGELOG: footer - grounded, not",
    "invented - then tagging normally. See plugins/ca-codex/CHANGELOG.md history",
    "for the reconstruction commit."
  ],
  "namespaces": [
    "v*",
    "ca-sandbox-v*",
    "ca-codex-v*",
    "ca-pi-v*"
  ],
